==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪz.əl/|/ˈmɪz.l̩/}}
* {{rhymes|ɪzəl}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|misellen||to drizzle|lang=enm}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nds|-}} {{term|musseln||to mizzle|lang=nds}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|miezelen||to drizzle, rain gently|lang=nl}}. Of obscure origin, but apparently related to {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|mes||urine|lang=de}}, {{etyl|dum|-}} {{term|mes|lang=dum}}, {{term|mis||urine|lang=dum}}, both from {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|mehs||urine|lang=osx}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*mihstuz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mihstaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mihsk-||urine}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*mīganą||to urinate}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*meiǵʰ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*omeiǵʰ-||to urinate}}. Compare also {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|micturate||to urinate|lang=en}}, {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term|mese||urine|lang=ofs}}, {{etyl|nds|-}} {{term|miegen||to urinate|lang=nds}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|mijgen||to urinate|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|mige||to urinate|lang=da}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|mizzl|ing}}

# {{context|intransitive|now|_|regional|UK|North America|lang=en}} To [[rain]] in very fine drops.

